    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0097" n="83" xml:id="pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.34/5–2444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-24">May 24, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Transfer of Naval Vessels to the Chinese
                    Government</p>
                <p>You will find attached a self-explanatory memorandum from Mr. Grew<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d75-f1"/> on the above subject. Also I am attaching a memorandum
                    from Mr. J. C. Vincent<anchor n="74" xml:id="d75-f2"/> and a confidential
                    memorandum submitted to me yesterday by Mr. Hornbeck.<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d75-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I don’t feel you need take the time to read these memoranda, but I feel this is a
                    matter you will wish to discuss briefly with Mr. Grew on your return to the
                    office. I feel it would be wise to proceed and that we should encourage this
                    transfer if the Navy can see their way clear to make the ships available. It is
                    more of a gesture at this moment than anything else. I think, as Dr. Hornbeck
                    ably points out, it will be a gesture towards strengthening our relations with
                    the Chinese Government particularly in their present difficult position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
